# Commit Style Rules — suparship

## Conventional Commits

All commits MUST follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format:

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

## Types

| Type | When to Use | Example |
|------|-------------|---------|
| `feat` | New feature | `feat(cli): add preview create command` |
| `fix` | Bug fix | `fix(renderer): handle empty values in templates` |
| `docs` | Documentation only | `docs: update installation guide` |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change | `style: run gofumpt on all files` |
| `refactor` | Code change, no new feature/fix | `refactor(gitops): extract ArgoCD client` |
| `test` | Adding/fixing tests | `test(renderer): add golden tests for service template` |
| `chore` | Maintenance, deps, CI | `chore: update golangci-lint to v1.55` |
| `perf` | Performance improvement | `perf(renderer): cache parsed templates` |
| `ci` | CI/CD changes | `ci: add security scanning workflow` |
| `build` | Build system changes | `build: update Go to 1.22` |
| `revert` | Revert previous commit | `revert: feat(cli): add preview create command` |

## Scopes

Use these scopes to indicate the affected area:

| Scope | Area |
|-------|------|
| `demo` | Demo command and sample app |
| `install` | Install command and profiles |
| `preview` | Preview environment functionality |
| `promote` | Promotion functionality |
| `cli` | General CLI (flags, output, UX) |
| `renderer` | Template rendering engine |
| `templates` | Template files |
| `gitops` | ArgoCD/Kargo integration |
| `k3d` | k3d cluster management |
| `security` | Security-related changes |
| `deps` | Dependency updates |

Scope is optional but recommended for non-trivial changes.

## Description Rules

### Format
- Start with lowercase verb
- No period at end
- Max 72 characters
- Imperative mood ("add" not "added" or "adds")

### Good Examples

```
feat(demo): add automatic port-forward for ArgoCD
fix(renderer): prevent duplicate resource names in output
docs(install): document --profile flag options
refactor(cli): extract common flag definitions
test(preview): add integration test for name sanitization
chore(deps): bump ArgoCD to v2.9.3
```

### Bad Examples

```
# Too vague
fix: fixed bug

# Past tense
feat(demo): added new feature

# Too long
feat(cli): add the ability for users to specify custom kubeconfig paths when running the install command

# No scope when one applies
feat: add preview command  # Should be feat(cli) or feat(preview)

# Capitalized
Feat(demo): Add new feature
```

## Body

Use body for:
- Explaining **why** (not what — the diff shows what)
- Providing context for complex changes
- Noting breaking changes

```
feat(install)!: change default namespace to suparship-system

The previous default namespace "suparship" conflicted with common
naming patterns. Moving to "suparship-system" follows Kubernetes
conventions for system components.

BREAKING CHANGE: Users upgrading must migrate resources from
"suparship" namespace or use --namespace flag explicitly.

Migration:
  kubectl get all -n suparship -o yaml > backup.yaml
  suparship install --reset --yes
```

## Footer

### Breaking Changes

Mark breaking changes with `!` after type/scope AND include `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer:

```
feat(cli)!: rename --env flag to --environment

BREAKING CHANGE: The --env flag is now --environment for clarity.
Update any scripts using --env to use --environment instead.
```

### Issue References

Reference issues in footer:

```
fix(renderer): handle nil pointer in template execution

The renderer would panic when a template referenced an undefined
variable. Now returns a clear error message.

Fixes #123
Closes #124
Related to #100
```

## Commit Granularity

### One Logical Change Per Commit

```
# GOOD: Separate commits
feat(cli): add --dry-run flag to install command
test(cli): add tests for install --dry-run
docs(cli): document --dry-run flag

# BAD: Mixed concerns
feat(cli): add --dry-run flag, fix typo in help, update deps
```

### When to Squash

Squash when:
- Multiple "fixup" commits during PR review
- WIP commits that don't stand alone
- Commits that break the build individually

Keep separate when:
- Each commit is a logical, atomic change
- Commits could be reverted independently
- History is useful for understanding evolution

## Examples by Area

### Demo Changes

```
feat(demo): add sample todo application
feat(demo): enable automatic browser open after setup
fix(demo): handle existing k3d cluster gracefully
chore(demo): update sample app image to v1.2.0
```

### Install Changes

```
feat(install): add --profile=full with monitoring stack
fix(install): wait for CRDs before creating resources
perf(install): parallelize component installation
refactor(install): extract helm operations to separate package
```

### Template Changes

```
feat(templates): add service-v2 template with HPA support
fix(templates): ensure deterministic YAML key ordering
test(templates): add golden tests for all templates
docs(templates): document template input format
```

### GitOps Changes

```
feat(gitops): generate Kargo Stage resources
fix(gitops): correct ArgoCD sync-wave annotations
refactor(gitops): use typed clients for ArgoCD resources
```

## Changelog Generation

Commits following this style enable automatic changelog generation:

```bash
# Generate changelog (example with git-cliff)
git-cliff --unreleased --tag v0.2.0
```

### Changelog Categories

| Commit Type | Changelog Section |
|-------------|-------------------|
| `feat` | ✨ Features |
| `fix` | 🐛 Bug Fixes |
| `perf` | ⚡ Performance |
| `docs` | 📚 Documentation |
| `refactor` | ♻️ Refactoring |
| `test` | ✅ Tests |
| `ci`, `chore`, `build` | 🔧 Maintenance |
| Breaking changes | 💥 Breaking Changes |

## Pre-Commit Validation

Consider adding commit-msg hook:

```bash
#!/bin/sh
# .git/hooks/commit-msg

commit_msg=$(cat "$1")
pattern='^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore|perf|ci|build|revert)(\([a-z-]+\))?!?: .{1,72}$'

if ! echo "$commit_msg" | head -1 | grep -qE "$pattern"; then
    echo "ERROR: Commit message doesn't follow Conventional Commits format"
    echo "Expected: <type>(<scope>): <description>"
    echo "Got: $(echo "$commit_msg" | head -1)"
    exit 1
fi
```

Or use [commitlint](https://commitlint.js.org/) in CI:

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yaml
- name: Lint commit messages
  uses: wagoid/commitlint-github-action@v5
```
